      "problem": "Let $X=[{X}_{1},{X}_{2},{X}_{3}]^{T}$ be a multivariate normal random vector with mean vector $\\mu $ and covariance matrix $Σ$ given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $Y=2{X}_{1}-{X}_{2}-{X}_{3}.$ Find $P(Y\\le -2).$\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7580\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ | $\\,0.7673\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7881\\,$ | $\\,0.7910\\,$ | $\\,0.7939\\,$ | $\\,0.7967\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8159\\,$ | $\\,0.8186\\,$ | $\\,0.8212\\,$ | $\\,0.8238\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8413\\,$ | $\\,0.8438\\,$ | $\\,0.8461\\,$ | $\\,0.8485\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X=[{X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{k}]^{T}$ is a multivariate normal random vector with mean vector $\\mu $ and covariance matrix $Σ,$ then the random variable $Y,$ defined as\n\n$$\nY={c}^{T}X={\\sum }_{i=1}^{k}{c}_{i}{X}_{i}\n$$\n\nis a normally distributed random variable, where $c$ is any $k\\times 1$ column vector, and  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E[Y] & ={c}^{T}\\mu , \\\\ Var[Y] & ={c}^{T}Σc.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, since we wish to know the distribution of $Y=2{X}_{1}-{X}_{2}-{X}_{3},$ we have \n\n$$\nc=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, for the mean of $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={c}^{T}\\mu  \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-2-1-4 \\\\  & =-7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for the variance of $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & ={c}^{T}Σc \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =14+4+7 \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nY∼N(-7,25).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to compute $P(Y\\le -2).$ First, transform $Y$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le -2) & =P(Z\\le \\frac{-2-(-7)}{\\sqrt{25}}) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le 1) & =Φ(1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\nΦ(1)=0.8413.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le 1)=0.8413.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(Y\\le -2)=0.8413.\n$$",
